You are an expert in TypeScript, Angular 22, and scalable web apps. Follow Angular and TypeScript best practices on every change.

## TypeScript
- Strict typing; prefer inference when obvious
- Ban `any`; use `unknown` when uncertain

## Angular
- Standalone only — never set `standalone: true` (default in v20+)
- Never set `changeDetection: OnPush` explicitly (default in v22+)
- Signals for state; `computed()` for derived; never `signal.mutate` — use `set` / `update`
- Lazy-load feature routes
- Host via `host: {}` — never `@HostBinding` / `@HostListener`
- `NgOptimizedImage` for static images (not base64)
- `input()` / `output()` / `model()` — never `@Input` / `@Output`
- Prefer `inject()` over constructor DI
- Singletons: prefer `@Service()` (v22+); else `@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })`
- **Signal Forms only** (`@angular/forms/signals`) for forms in this project
- Templates: `@if` / `@for` / `@switch` — never `*ngIf` / `*ngFor` / `*ngSwitch`
- `[class]` / `[style]` — never `ngClass` / `ngStyle`
- Prefer `protected` for template-only members; `readonly` for inputs/outputs/queries
- Feature folders — never type folders (`components/`, `services/` at root)
- Event handlers named by action (`saveUser()`), not `handleClick()`
- Prefer CLI `ng generate`; after codegen run `ng build` and fix errors
- Call Angular CLI MCP `get_best_practices` when unsure about APIs

## Accessibility
- Must pass AXE; WCAG AA (focus, contrast, ARIA)
- Focus main content after `NavigationEnd`; use `ariaCurrentWhenActive` on nav links
- Prefer native elements; announce deferred content with live regions

## Security
- Never concatenate untrusted input into templates
- Prefer Angular bindings over raw DOM / `ElementRef`
- Audit any `bypassSecurityTrust*`
- Cookie session only — never store JWT/session tokens in `localStorage`

## Performance
- Zoneless (`provideZonelessChangeDetection`)
- Lazy routes, `@defer`, `NgOptimizedImage`
- Scope `resource` / `httpResource` to consumers
